{"event_type":"review","id":"cbcb164b12bb96a4e07fd558b3e91d33253a8d58a7ac0c78a8c0a0dadd15b38f","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T04:41:26Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5a98ef8be8817ee00f3e147e61a9f2de60ae1f2416358a46ed48474fce1fc158","sha256":"5a98ef8be8817ee00f3e147e61a9f2de60ae1f2416358a46ed48474fce1fc158"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a1ce07056caba89c8ec453285fc71ca58b98b8202d2b802a8b78a5eb55847c20","sha256":"a1ce07056caba89c8ec453285fc71ca58b98b8202d2b802a8b78a5eb55847c20"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/175bf2f9adbadc6cea4b4d7e3db1d71665f03fdce0e5b5c08265c641d006d4df","sha256":"175bf2f9adbadc6cea4b4d7e3db1d71665f03fdce0e5b5c08265c641d006d4df"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1bbff031a80d5253e3d155660c483a0f4442841159e79fda5db84151c9ba5ce1","sha256":"1bbff031a80d5253e3d155660c483a0f4442841159e79fda5db84151c9ba5ce1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6b0dbe87af2a279018368f878667750618409aab1d8a582cbb40bad151086a46","sha256":"6b0dbe87af2a279018368f878667750618409aab1d8a582cbb40bad151086a46"}],"attempt_id":"21c39d8d2a5c9530890adb826dad463a890a8ec94072879af2a2a91990a69814:0:1","base":"67717d3cd9e7664b3cf7d95a35eeb13c56e4dc1f","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"5ff9bfc90b71dcd66a83564fcb4bdbbf37aa91a9","body":"**Fix `stagedPathsOf` to fail closed on a truncated capture (src/ops/sweep/stagePaths.ts:84-93).**\n\nIf a record has a missing path token, line 90 silently skips it. This happens with a truncated capture or an unexpected status. The function then returns fewer paths, and `classifyStagePaths` can return `clean` without checking the dropped path. A rename with only the old path is one example: the new path is never checked.\n\nThe function also has no case for an unexpected record shape. For example, `-z` output can have a status token that is not a status. In that case the function consumes the next token as a path and loses alignment.\n\nMake the parser throw on a missing path token. The caller can then map the error onto `infra` or `failed`. This follows the doctrine that missing evidence is non-passing (I5).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     for (let n = 0; n < pathCount; n += 1) {\n       const path = tokens[index];\n-      if (path !== undefined) paths.push(path);\n+      if (path === undefined) {\n+        throw new Error(`malformed name-status capture: status '${status}' is missing a path`);\n+      }\n+      paths.push(path);\n       index += 1;\n     }\n```\n</details>","id":"ca89920fccb797847607d5c7a46bef2bee3ac130b44b51d4759dc86a9b916438","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/sweep/stagePaths.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Fix `stagedPathsOf` to fail closed on a truncated capture (src/ops/sweep/stagePaths.ts:84-93)."}],"head":"8a01b2c65d1babea9511c63cf64821759359499b","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"5ff9bfc90b71dcd66a83564fcb4bdbbf37aa91a9","intervals":[[1,95]],"path":"src/ops/sweep/stagePaths.ts"}],"job_id":"21c39d8d2a5c9530890adb826dad463a890a8ec94072879af2a2a91990a69814:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"5ff9bfc90b71dcd66a83564fcb4bdbbf37aa91a9","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/sweep/stagePaths.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"3aee477168e1da8e2aa232a98e80747d98da8f26f54f2a27e0c62d13e349d4b1","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"5ff9bfc90b71dcd66a83564fcb4bdbbf37aa91a9","intervals":[[1,95]],"path":"src/ops/sweep/stagePaths.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"5ff9bfc90b71dcd66a83564fcb4bdbbf37aa91a9","intervals":[[1,95]],"path":"src/o